This file explains what the databases could potentially look like.

## User DB
- format: JSON file
- note: tutorial mode is not saved to db.
- sample DB:
  - {"username_1": {
      "password": "string password",
      "ModeProgress": {
        "QuickMode": {
            "quickModeRoomsUnlocked": ["roomID_1", "roomID_2", ...],
            "quickModeItemInventory": {
                "roomID_1": ["itemID", ...],
                "roomID_2": [...]
            },
            "quickModeHintsWatched": {
                "roomID_1": {
                    "objectID_1": request_count(int),
                    "objectID_2": request_count(int),
                ...},
                "roomID_2": {...}
            }
        }
        "StoryMode": {
            "storyModeRoomsUnlocked": [...],
            "storyModeItemInventory": [...],
            "storyModeHintsWatched": {String, Integer},
            "storyModeCurrentRoomID": "roomID",
        }
      }
  }

      "username_2": {...}
  }


